{"skill":{"slug":"gitlab-cli-skills","displayName":"gitlab-cli-skills"},"version":{"version":"1.13.32","createdAt":1791905341080,"changelog":"glab v1.123.0: subgroup clone exclusions, guarded SSH-key replacement, issue time tracking, JSON API input, token registry-domain persistence, list totals/visibility, fail-closed Dependency Firewall, and curated remote Orbit skills. Includes all 10 validated review remediations.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":254953,"sha256":"1363f4f6cc67741270cef9144878433cd83336f70baceec906198f85d1b7e8fd","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2281,"sha256":"e7b1c1a7f56b2396a44921834d12c14b45b76825064756beddf5492460fd189e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1791906128445,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c37ecab4d356b9a8229fbc8b1df16ba57bb85f0e1c17df6d064b318512ca9e5b","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c37ecab4d356b9a8229fbc8b1df16ba57bb85f0e1c17df6d064b318512ca9e5b","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1791905807492},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":65,"checkedAt":1791906128445},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"medium","summary":"This is a broad GitLab CLI reference skill that does not run code by itself, but it documents powerful authenticated GitLab actions that users must apply carefully.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Use of GitLab credentials, env files, keyrings, package-manager auth files, and local config is proportionate for a GitLab CLI skill and is disclosed with secrecy and verification guidance. Orbit local indexing and governance transcript sync are sensitive but described with scope and approval warnings.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The packaged artifact inspected is a Markdown skill with a glab dependency and no bundled executable files. It references sibling skills and supporting references/scripts/templates that are not present in this package, and it documents glab commands that can install or update other agent skills, including a remote Orbit skill.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions are broad because the skill covers most GitLab CLI surfaces, including raw API calls, approvals, merges, deletes, token management, and bulk actions. The artifact repeatedly tells users to verify host, actor, target project, and destructive flags before writes.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill itself has no persistence, but it documents glab flows that can persist credentials, install managed binaries or skills, modify agent settings, and install a durable govern audit-sync job. Those behaviors are disclosed and tied to explicit setup/update commands.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is a comprehensive glab command reference, and the documented capabilities - authentication, merge requests, CI/CD, variables, runners, packages, skills, Orbit, and governance - fit that purpose. Many operations are high-impact, but they are presented as user-invoked GitLab workflows rather than hidden automation.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you want a broad glab reference and are comfortable with agents being guided through authenticated GitLab operations. Before using write, delete, approve, merge, variable, token, runner, secure-file, skills update/install, govern, or Orbit commands, verify the GitLab host, account, project/group, and any upload or persistence scope. Treat govern transcript sync and Orbit/skills remote installs as separate high-trust actions requiring explicit review.","findings":"[PE3] expected: Credential and token references are expected for a GitLab CLI authentication and automation reference. The artifact discusses env files, keyrings, artifact-registry tokens, package-manager auth files, and CI/CD variables while warning not to print, commit, or misuse secrets; I found no artifact-backed credential exfiltration behavior.\n[AE1] unexpected: The package references sibling skills and supporting files such as references/commands.md, scripts, and templates that are not present in the inspected artifact. This limits documentation completeness, but the available SKILL.md is analyzable and the missing references do not show hidden execution or deception.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1791906128445}}}}}